@0    = ~I can hear so many spirits here. Everything - all these voices, these energies, whirling. This place has much to tell, <CHARNAME>.~
@1    = ~Can you understand what they're saying?~
@2    = ~Let's not keep them waiting.~
@3    = ~No... they wish to speak with you alone, no one else. Do you believe Ellesime was right? Can they tell you about everything that is happening... about you, your heritage and the other Bhaalspawn?~
@4    = ~I don't know, but I hope so. That's why I'm here, after all.~
@5    = ~I only came so that people would finally shut up. I don't want to hear one more person telling me things like: "You should give it a try!"~
@6    = ~Maybe. Let's just hear them out, alright?~
@7    = ~Right. We'd best be quick, I think it may start raining soon.~
@8    = ~Right, well, we're already here, for good or ill. Perhaps you'll find out something new.~
@9    = ~Right.~
@10   = ~So Irenicus - what was left of him - was sent to Hell. Bodhi crumbled to dust. Suldanessellar... the Tree of Life... they're all safe, at least for now.~
@11   = ~I can tell something's troubling you, Will. What's wrong?~
@12   = ~All is as it should be, and the Tree of Life is the responsiblity of elves from Suldanessellar. Let's let them take it all back into their own hands.~
@13   = ~Will, we have new foes and very little time to prepare a good plan. You may stay in my group, but let's cut our discussions.~
@14   = ~There actually was something, in fact.~
@15   = ~Yes, they certainly should learn from what's happened... they should figure out how to better protect the Tree and reorganize everything after what has happened.~
@16   = ~But... there is one thing I just can't get out of my mind.~
@17   = ~Do you remember that moment when we found the Exile and Ellesime caged? Right after killing the parasites that fed on the Tree of Life?~
@18   = ~Of course I do. Why?~
@19   = ~I do, but Will - now's really not the time. I understand you have some thoughts about what's going on, but remember we have some huge responsibilities. We should focus on our mission, not our retrospections or doubts. We should move on.~
@20   = ~Joneleth and Ellesime - there was something between them. A past that really mattered to them, perhaps even then. I think that, when I heard them talk, I saw a moment of doubt in Irenicus. I did not expect him to feel anything other than hatred or wrath, but for a tiny moment he felt... different.~
@21   = ~That might have been the case, but he deserved what he got nonetheless.~
@22   = ~I know what you mean, as I had the same feeling. Perhaps he did truly love Ellesime, and considered her banishment of him as a betrayal.~
@23   = ~We don't have time for such thoughts now, Will. Might we move on?~
@24   = ~Yes, I agree that he did... but it's still a comfort to know even a man like the Exile could have felt more than his lust for power or vengeance.~
@25   = ~You may be right. Perhaps he also bore wounds that never truly healed.~
@26   = ~Do you think Ellesime could have stopped him from doing everything he did? Long before you encountered him for the first time?~
@27   = ~Of course! She could have simply executed him instead of setting him free with all of his power.~
@28   = ~Perhaps. If there was anyone who held any influence over Irenicus, it was Ellesime herself.~
@29   = ~I doubt it. He obeyed nothing but his sick mind and twisted ambitions. Even Bodhi was nothing more than a tool to him.~
@30   = ~We have no time for this, Will. We should move on. I'd rather you not bother me with this again.~
@31   = ~You think that was the only way? Perhaps you're right. He could never have been influenced, only stopped. There may be those who were born solely to become threats to the living with their ideas and ambitions. Still, the thought is rather sad.~
@32   = ~Would their love have allowed them to listen to each other? They must have spoken before Irenicus was banished. Perhaps Ellesime even knew of his plan, attempted to change his mind, but failed. She may have given up, or... or he had already gone too far, before she realized it.~
@33   = ~Yes... I almost forgot about Bodhi's place in that whole affair. Was it not her who supported his madness? Even some of the elves believed that she corrupted Irenicus and encouraged him to attempt to become a god. I doubt such a revelation, assuming it was true, would surprise me much considering her twisted character.~
@34   = ~Regardless, I think we should get back to current affairs. I only hope we may stop our future foes just as we stopped the Exile.~
@35   = ~That's what we've always done. We'll succeed again.~
@36   = ~We won't find out by standing here. Come on, let's get them.~
@37   = ~Right. But before we move on - I really want us to cut our conversations here. We should waste no more time on pointless babbling. I hope you get what I mean.~
@38   = ~Right. We've done it before, so... anyways, we should get moving now. We can find time to talk later..~
@39   = ~Right. I'm right behind you, <CHARNAME>.~
@40   = ~I won't bother you again, then. I suppose I want to end it all as soon as possible.~
@41   = ~Do you think Athkatla has changed since we were there?~
@42   = ~Why would it have changed?~
@43   = ~I have no idea, to be honest.~
@44   = ~It must have changed a little. So many things happened during the time we were there, right?~
@45   = ~You know, I don't really care. I don't want to spend my time discussing it.~
@46   = ~Because you affected many people in that time. We destroyed Bodhi and her guild, supported those who you believed that deserved it. All those actions must have had some consequences.~
@47   = ~I see. Perhaps it's hard for you to focus on a distant place while being away from it, stopping another nightmare from becoming a reality.~
@48   = ~Right. The destruction of Bodhi, the fall of her guild... perhaps even the events of Spellhold may have influenced the Cowled Wizards.~
@49   = ~Perhaps you will know the same feelings I had. When you return to a place you once new, it will have become a brand new place, with different people, different leaders, new problems, even a new culture. It seems like every place touched by your hand reshapes itself in some way. The Visionhive, Athkatla - even the Hells. You were able to make it your Pocket Plane, weren't you?~
@50   = ~I believe that many spirits will whisper about you, your actions and your powers for years. Perhaps they wil continue past your lifetime. I was wondering if you are the trigger that the Realms have been waiting for, so that they may be transformed.~
@51   = ~The question is if such changes will be for the better, or the opposite.~
@52   = ~If I did not believe change, I wouldn't have done all those things. I wanted to see a different tomorrow and I'll be happy to what comes.~
@53   = ~I don't want be the only cause of change. If something's going to "transform", as you suggest, then I can only pray I am not the sole cause of it all.~
@54   = ~Who knows. One can only hope that the changes will be good.~
@55   = ~I hope you'll enjoy the view when tomorrow comes.~
@56   = ~True, I suppose there is always more than one factor. Though you may have forced some changes with your actions - killing Bodhi, for example - there will always be others who may or may not take advantage of the results. But you were the once who created such circumstances.~
@57   = ~What do you think of yourself? Do you think you have changed much?~
@58   = ~I never had time to think much about how much I've changed, Will. I guess I must have, but I don't think I know how much.~
@59   = ~I haven't changed. I am still the <PRO_MANWOMAN> that Gorion raised. No matter how much stronger I've become, or how many bruises I've gotten, I still follow the same ideals.~
@60   = ~Well, I realized that Irenicus was right when he said there was much unlocked potential inside me. I've changed. I've unlocked my true self.~
@61   = ~I think I've gotten much sexier with all this hair I've grown my chest! Hehe.~
@62   = ~I haven't changed. I don't want to change. Why should I, when I am satisfied with who I am?~
@63   = ~I don't know. But can we finally move on? We have no time for this.~
@64   = ~I see.~
@65   = ~Let's hope a fireball won't burn it then.~
@66   = ~Anyway, I apologize if I've gotten into philosophical tones again. I believe we should move on, right?~
@67   = ~It's alright. You know I like talking to you. But you're right, we should be moving now.~
@68   = ~Stow it and let us do our work rather than bothering me with nonexistent problems.~
@69   = ~I'll be right behind you.~
@70   = ~I'm sorry to have troubled you. Just calm down and give your orders.~
@71   = ~I find it a little disturbing to think that so many of your siblings have allowed themselves to be controlled by their blood. I think that only proves you have a strength they do not.~
@72   = ~It's not just the matter of blood. As I recall, you once said I am only what I am, and my blood does not dictate me.~
@73   = ~I don't want to talk about this right now. We should move on.~
@74   = ~I still believe that. I think it's the other Bhaalspawn that believe otherwise. They believe their blood entitles them to greatness and the right to do what they desire. But they never had that right despite what blood they possess.~
@75   = ~That is why they must be stopped. Or do you think there is more to it than that?~
@76   = ~I can see their point of view. If they truly had the power to take what they want, then they deserve it more than others. But if they try to take anything of mine, I'll send them to join Illasera in the grave.~
@77   = ~I don't care what you, or anyone else thinks. Stop wasting my time.~
@78   = ~I think so. Do you think you will ever have the chance to decide your own fate? Will these threats of attack on you for your blood ever end?~
@79   = ~I'm sure of it.~
@80   = ~I hope so. I'm sick of having my actions dicated for me. I want to choose my own future one day.~
@81   = ~Actually... I'm not so sure I want it all to end.~
@82   = ~You really believe that? Power alone shouldn't decide what you're allowed to do. If you alone possessed a sword, should you have the right to kill anyone you wished? I don't think so.~
@83   = ~I disagree. You should be able to do anything within your power. That is what freedom is.~
@84   = ~I guess you're right. But we can't expect everyone to follow the same rules. After all, aren't we also forced to slay anyone that disagrees with us?~
@85   = ~This discussion is a pointless waste of time. Go bother someone else.~
@86   = ~Heh, it's good that you still hold some hope within you. I couldn't hope for much more.~
@87   = ~I guess I overlooked that option.~
@88   = ~That's an honest answer, if rather crude. I can't deny there's some truth to that. We should try to exceed our limits, but using power as a means to acquire freedom can be destructive.~
@89   = ~Anyways... I just wanted to say that... even despite the crooked and twisted road we follow, I'm still relieved to know you know what you're doing, and why you're doing it. I wonder if those that raised you knew how skilled of a leader you would become.~
@90   = ~Gorion and my mentors prepared me well for the world beyond Candlekeep.~
@91   = ~I needed to learn for myself. I felt that was the best way to survive; mastering the road by experience.~
@92   = ~Whatever. Let's get moving.~
@93   = ~I guess they really knew what they were doing then.~
@94   = ~It's a dangerous way, but apparently it gets results.~
@95   = ~I guess I shouldn't have bothered you to begin with.~
@96   = ~I've... been having some troubles on my mind, <CHARNAME>. If you would give me your honest opinion... I would appreciate it. I hold your thoughts in high regard.~
@97   = ~I'm all ears. What's wrong, my friend?~
@98   = ~I'm sure you could conjure up a spirit if you needed a friend to talk to. I've got no time for you.~
@99   = ~I should start from the beginning... I've asked you many things, about fate, about Irenicus, and about everything that has happened since we've met. Most importantly... we've talked about change.~
@100  = ~As I am now... I cannot change. I will neither grow nor age, nor begin a new life. I fear the day that our adventures together must truly come to an end. What shall I do if that day comes?~
@101  = ~You should've told me sooner that you've been considering this. I never realized how much the end of this must mean to you.~
@102  = ~Perhaps you should begin a new adventure on your own? With a group of your own, even?~
@103  = ~Why can't you start anew? Can you truly find no place to call home?~
@104  = ~I don't mean to be cruel, but... is it not possible for you to finally rest in peace?~
@105  = ~It means everything to me. Perhaps it is less so for you, or everyone around you, but... to me, the end means to meet silence... to meet the void.~
@106  = ~I... doubt the dead are meant for such things. I know I made an exception for you, but it was out of gratitude for everything you did for the land - for the Visionhive. When this story ends, there'll be nothing... truly nothing left for me.~
@107  = ~The only home I have ever known was the Visionhive. But if I return there, then it is but silence by another fate. Returning there will not be easy after everything I have experienced and learned at your side, my friend.~
@108  = ~I... I don't know. I really don't.~
@109  = ~Perhaps you know of the Fugue Plane, where the dead travel to wait in judgment. That should have been my fate, but I became... stuck inbetween this plane and the next. I slept in the Visionhive for years, and now I have walked this plane for months. I am not wise in the Planes, but... I somehow doubt I can easily transit to the Fugue Plane now... as I am.~
@110  = ~There might still be a way. Anything's possible.~
@111  = ~Perhaps you could search for someone who could unbind you from this Realm? As I recall, followers of Kelemvor know much of the Fugue Plane.~
@112  = ~I fear you will need to embrace what you have become, Will. You've already gained much for someone who should already be long gone.~
@113  = ~This is far from my concern right now. I can't help you, and I don't particularly care to.~
@114  = ~It's optimistic of you to believe there might still be a good solution to this.~
@115  = ~I hope not, but you may be right. There might truly be no solution but to accept the coldness and silence of nothingness.~
@116  = ~Still, I assure you - no matter what the future might be for me, I will remain and fight at your side for as long as you demand. That is all I care about right now. My fate is secondary so long as I may still help free you from your own bindings.~
@117  = ~Thank you, Will.~
@118  = ~Right. In that case, let's get going.~
@119  = ~You have nothing to thank me for, <CHARNAME>.~
@120  = ~I'm right behind you.~
@121  = ~I'm sorry I ever bothered you.~
@122  = ~Do you believe I made the right decision when I chose to leave Visionhive, <PRO_BROTHERSISTER>?~
@123  = ~For me, yes. I felt I needed you then, and I definitely need you now. I might've died long ago without you.~
@124  = ~I don't know. I doubt I could ever understand how you felt about leaving.~
@125  = ~What do I care? Think on it in silence if you must at all.~
@126  = ~So you do believe my leaving of the grotto must have been justified, right?~
@127  = ~I felt that if I did not see your world, the one I was once part of, I would be poorer for lacking the experience. But at the same time, I wouldn't end up missing all these wonders we've seen together if I have never left.~
@128  = ~The day I joined you for the first time doesn't seem distant to me. My mind as it is can remember days long ago, so that memory is as close as the blink of an eye. And now we're so close to the end of your tale. But even if, to me, we have not known each other for long... this brief time has been the most valuable in my entire existence.~
@129  = ~And now it's so close... so close to the end.~
@130  = ~It'll all be alright. There is no end to the wonders of this world. Even if you can't experience life as mortals can, you can see more than any of us. Your gift of Sight could guide many living men to victory. You don't need life to be important to others.~
@131  = ~Why are you so certain our tale will end once all this is over? Our adventures can surely continue even beyond this.~
@132  = ~Will... you of all people should understand that things end. Otherwise, nothing would serve a purpose. Our experiences are valuable because we know they won't last. I know it's difficult, but... we must accept it. Just remember everything - from the times we shared to the foes we prevailed over.~
@133  = ~Oh, would you quit your whining? All you're saying is how terrible the end will be. You're worse than Xan! Let's just move on and be done with it!~
@134  = ~That's true, but... I wonder if I really want to start anything new. Perhaps it would be better just to let go. If I choose to seek other adventures, then... I will only be running from what I have become... what I am.~
@135  = ~Even so, an end must come eventually. I would only be postponing it one way or another. I have no doubt our adventures will soon end. It may be in a week, or it may be in a few months. To you, that may be a long time, but... to me, that's only a short instant. I must think of what to do next.~
@136  = ~You show your wisdom once again. Yes... I should remember it all.~
@137  = ~I asked you of the Visionhive before because... I am not sure if I will be able to unite with it again.~
@138  = ~In my journey with you, I have changed, and I have no doubt the grotto will have as well. Our spirits may no longer sing in unison, and if so, we may not be able to rebuild the connection we once had. If so... what then? Is all that is left for me nothingness and stagnation?~
@139  = ~Do you really think that's possible?~
@140  = ~That's your problem, not mine. I'm getting sick of all of your "what-if" scenarios that you enjoy so much.~
@141  = ~I'm afraid so, yes. It's a possibility, and a high one at that.~
@142  = ~I never even considered that might be the case.~
@143  = ~Don't believe that will be the only option. I never do, after all.~
@144  = ~Think on it on your own, and don't bother me with it again.~
@145  = ~For the longest time, neither did I.~
@146  = ~I don't think I can do that. It'd be like asking a mountain to change its position. We both know that's impossible.~
@147  = ~Thank you for listening, at least. Talking with you has helped relieve some of my worries. I don't expect a solution from you. I just wanted to know you were here for me, as you always have been.~
@148  = ~If there's anything else you needed to discuss, anything at all... I'm here.~
@149  = ~You're welcome.~
@150  = ~Then you've wasted my time. If this comes up again then just... leave me out of it. I'm done with you.~
@151  = ~No, it's fine... thank you. There are some things that I must think on alone. We should move on anyways.~
@152  = ~You've been a good friend to me, <CHARNAME>.~
@153  = ~Is that so? Fine then, if that's your decision. I won't bother you again.~
@154  = ~It's so close to the end. We've triumphed over all our battles but this last one. We've made it so far now... and I want to see you win, <PRO_BROTHERSISTER>. You will, I'm certain of it.~
@155  = ~Thank you, Will. I can't deny that I'm a little frightened.~
@156  = ~I know I will. There is no other option.~
@157  = ~We have no time for this, Will. My destiny awaits us.~
@158  = ~I understand. I'm a little frightened myself, knowing what powers we are soon to face. They may be great enough to annihilate me instantly - a fate worse than death. I would be erased entirely.~
@159  = ~It's good to see that you never lose your confidence, even when the stakes are highest, my friend. We'll both have need of that strength.~
@160  = ~<CHARNAME>...~
@161  = ~Hmm?~
@162  = ~Let's cut the small talk. We must focus on what's left to do.~
@163  = ~I said before that I was worried about this story ending, because nothing more awaits me. But despite that, I want to help you end this. I'll be happy to do anything so long as it is at your side. I'm glad I met you. It is one thing I shall never regret.~
@164  = ~Thank you, Will. I wouldn't have made it this far without the support of my friends. Including you.~
@165  = ~It's been my honor to share your company as well, Will.~
@166  = ~Look, don't get sentimental. Our adventure's about to end anyway.~
@167  = ~Heh... I guess we got a bit too sentimental again.~
@168  = ~I've accepted the silence that will come later. Anything else would just be running away. I will find a way to finally rest in peace. Perhaps, in the silence, I may even hear the voice of my beloved Higam. Heh... that would surely comfort me, allow me to...~
@169  = ~...anyways, thank you. Again... for everything. I will soon face the void, but first... let's make sure you are victorious.~
@170  = ~Thank you. I know you'll find the peace you're looking for. Now let's end this together.~
@171  = ~Whatever. Come on, we're so close to finishing this.~
@172  = ~Then that's just what we'll do. Together.~
@173  = ~You're right. It's almost over.~
@174  = ~They're all dead. All that were trapped in Saradush are dead. The city can never be the same again.~
@175  = ~I wish we could have done something more.~
@176  = ~It's a huge tragedy. If only we could've prevented it, whether by stopping Yaga-Shura sooner or... or somehow influencing Gromnir... maybe they would still be alive.~
@177  = ~I don't want to talk about this. Now give me some space, Will, I don't have time for you right now.~
@178  = ~I'm afraid that we did all we could. From now on this land will wail as banshees do. It will be tainted with cries of pain and loss.~
@179  = ~It reminds me of Dragonspear Castle. I just hope this disaster won't cause any new incarnations of terror and death.~
@180  = ~I suppose even I have my limits. I stopped a war. I killed Irenicus. Faced the threats in Nine Hells, but this - this I failed to prevent.~
@181  = ~I don't want to talk about this. Let's move on.~
@182  = ~I weren't there with you during the Dragonspear siege, but many spirits whispered to me about what happened in the Castle and nearby lands. About all the blood and despair.~
@183  = ~We all have our limits... We can't save everyone.~
@184  = ~This massacre here, in Saradush - it's but another scar in the history of the realms we live in. I will whisper tonight, while you sleep, to calm all the spirits, all the crying beings that were slaughtered. That's better than nothing, right? I'm not sure if I can do anything else.~
@185  = ~Calm them down, Will. They may listen to you.~
@186  = ~Calm them down, Will, and tell them that we will avenge them. We won't stop at killing Yaga-Shura. We'll kill everyone that was on his side.~
@187  = ~Eh, just mourn them in silence, will you? We should be going.~
@188  = ~That's what I'll tell them. But if I could, I would kill Yaga-Shura over and over again, until he knows the same number of deaths that he and his army caused.~
@189  = ~That's quite vengeful of you.~
@190  = ~I know the feeling. I would do the same... he should die a thousand times and suffer even more than that.~
@191  = ~I don't want to discuss this any longer. We should be moving.~
@192  = ~He should have rotted alive. But at least he won't hurt anyone now.~
@193  = ~Because I am not sure I can easily accept someone could kill so many people, just like that.~
@194  = ~I'm sorry, I guess we should move on. I think I need to calm down.~
@195  = ~(Will remains in silence for a while) Let's move on, <CHARNAME>. I think I need some time to calm down. I'll be right behind you.~
@196  = ~Fine.~
@197  = ~I think her mind must be corrupted. She has lost her sanity long ago, and I'm not sure she can help us in *any* way.~
@198  = ~Death cannot be held at bay forever, giant! Spirits already whisper tales of your doom!~
@199  = ~He may be telling the truth. I can hear some unusual whispers coming from the dark, <CHARNAME>.~
@200  = ~Sendai... you have ended far too many lives. I can hear the voices of the dead screaming your name. All the weeping, all the hatred... ~
@201  = ~I care nothing of the past, ghost. You are a killer as much as I. Silence!~
@202  = ~I believe no one should tell you what to decide, <CHARNAME>. Nor dead, nor the living. This is your decision to make, my friend.~
@203  = ~Do you have anything to say about Will?~
@204  = ~Will, the mysterious spectre that follow you, yes? Well, how could I forget about him?~
@205  = ~Where... ah, yes, it's here: Will, the enigmatic entity helps <CHARNAME> in <PRO_HISHER> adventures. He can see more than any living man, for he hears the voices of spirits, and <CHARNAME> could find no finer advisor either living or unliving. His past may be unknown, yet with his power, he may bring a ghastly end to those who stand on his and <CHARNAME>'s way.~
@206  = ~Thank you, but... while I believe you had good intentions writing this, never have I been that bloodthirsty.~
